# ★★★ SUBTARGET (interaptiv) OVERRIDE OF THE SHARED wireless CONFIG -- ONE
# DIFFERENCE ONLY: radio0 ships DISABLED, as a TEMPORARY hold.
#
# MEASURED 2026-08-27 on the LANLY G24W, twice (transcript
# results/artifacts/uboot_tftp/RTL9603CVD/LANLY/G24W/2026-08-27.log): the FIRST
# wlan0 open -- possible at all only since wifi-scripts landed -- ends the boot.
#   boot 1: rtl92fe_hw_init -> pcie_capability_* -> panic (__initconst chip
#           table under a lifetime pointer; FIXED in pcie-rtl960x.c);
#   boot 2, with that fixed: hostapd opens wlan0 at ~21 s and the single CPU
#           livelocks in softirq ("watchdog: BUG: soft lockup - CPU#0 stuck for
#           26s! [hostapd:1354]"), panic at 48 s, SoC watchdog full-chip reset,
#           U-Boot autoboots the committed STOCK image.
# The signature is a stuck level PCIe INTx re-entered forever on one core. The
# vendor's own 9603cvd_pci.c does NO bridge-side interrupt ack, so this is not
# a one-register host-bridge fix; it needs its own sitting (which line storms,
# /proc/interrupts with the open triggered by hand on a live console).
#
# WHY HERE and not a uci-default: netifd's first wireless bring-up races
# uci_apply_defaults (measured: hostapd's open at ~21 s vs defaults finishing
# ~21 s), so only the SHIPPED file loses no race. This subtarget builds the
# G24W and the RTL9607C engboard; the engboard has no phy0 (no chip entry in
# pcie-rtl960x.c binds its PCIe), so the hold is G24W-scoped in practice.
#
# REMOVE THIS FILE the day the storm is fixed -- the shared target file then
# ships again, byte-identical minus this hold. wifi_ap_onair keeps FAILING
# while this hold stands, and that is CORRECT: the AP truly is not on air.
#
# ★★ A CANDIDATE FIX EXISTS AS OF 2026-09-01, AND IT IS ONU-SIDE -- which is
# what the paragraph above predicted when it said this is NOT a one-register
# host-bridge fix.  Three coupled repairs, all in the SHARED rtlwifi driver
# this subtarget and the X111W both build:
#   * _rtl_pci_interrupt() returned IRQ_HANDLED on two paths that touch NO
#     endpoint register, so the ISR was never write-1-to-cleared, DEASSERT_INTx
#     was never sent, and the level stayed asserted.  It returns IRQ_NONE now.
#   * rtl92fe_enable_interrupt() armed HIMR/HIMRE BEFORE setting irq_enabled,
#     so an assertion arriving in that window met a handler that refused to
#     service it.  The flag leads now; the disarm is read-back-flushed.
#   * the X111W's PCIe INTC input was 15 where every other source says 16.
#     (That one is 9602C-scoped and does not touch this board.)
# Upstream describes the same race for this driver family: "rtlwifi: rtl8192x:
# Enabling and disabling hardware interrupts after enabling local irq flags".
#
# ⚠ DO NOT DELETE THIS FILE ON THE STRENGTH OF THAT.  The fix is BUILT and
# UNPROVEN -- no board has booted it.  The order is: boot the X111W with it
# (that board dies silently rather than printing, so it is the harder test),
# then boot THIS board with the hold still in place and open wlan0 BY HAND on
# a live console while watching /proc/interrupts.  Only a G24W that survives
# that open earns the deletion, and `disabled '1'` is what keeps a failed
# attempt from costing a watchdog reset into stock.
#   guard: python3 ONU-test-case/irq_claim_order_guard.py
config wifi-device 'radio0'
	option type 'mac80211'
	option phy 'phy0'
	option channel '1'
	option band '2g'
	option htmode 'HT20'
	option country 'BO'
	option disabled '1'

config wifi-iface 'default_radio0'
	option device 'radio0'
	option network 'lan'
	option mode 'ap'
	option multicast_to_unicast '1'
	# ssid + key are overwritten per-board at boot by /etc/uci-defaults/99-onu-wifi.
	option ssid 'ONU-X111W-AP'
	option encryption 'psk2'
	option key '12345678'
